  "review_summary": "Independent pedagogical and physics verification of 9702_s19_42 Question 2 is clean with 0 findings. Part (a)(i) correctly identifies +q as energy transferred to the system by heating and +w as work done on the system. Part (a)(ii) identifies negative Delta U as decrease in internal energy. Part (b)(i) clearly explains that total Delta U is 0 because the gas returns to its initial state and temperature after a complete cycle. Part (b)(ii) calculates external work done on the gas during expansion as -240 J using W = -p Delta V. Part (b)(iii) accurately populates all thermodynamic cycle values in Fig. 2.2 table. All hints, walkthroughs, rubrics, and curriculum mappings are sound.",
